# Nothing bounds how deep the function calls itself, so it checks the stack once where it sets its frame up.
# CHECK: f1: size={{*}} prologueChecks=1
# CHECK-NOT: enteredWithoutStackCheck
# CHECK: f{{*}}: size=
# The call may end in the error for a full stack, so it may leave sideways. Nothing behind it asks whether it threw.
# B3-LABEL: name="depth" role=Source
# B3: Int64 b@[[follower]] = Load(b@{{*}}, offset = 16, ControlDependent|Reads:ObjectFields{{*}}:GetSlot)
# B3-NEXT: Double b@[[rest]] = Patchpoint(b@[[follower]]:Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = Register({{*}}), ExitsSideways|{{*}}:CallDirect)
# B3-NOT: Branch(
# B3-NOT: Patchpoint(
# B3: Double b@{{*}} = Add(b@[[rest]], 
# B3-LABEL: end of function
# The frame, and the check with it, belongs to the arm that calls. The end of the list answers without either.
# X64-LABEL: name="depth" role=Source
# X64-NEXT: BB#0:
# X64-NEXT: Branch64 Equal, %{{*}}, $2
# X64: EnterFrame
# X64-NOT: EnterFrame
# X64: Patch &Patchpoint
# X64: LeaveFrame
# X64-NOT: Frame
# X64-LABEL: end of function
# ARM64-LABEL: name="depth" role=Source
# ARM64-NEXT: BB#0:
# ARM64-NEXT: Branch64 Equal, %{{*}}, $2
# ARM64: EnterFrame
# ARM64-NOT: EnterFrame
# ARM64: Patch &Patchpoint
# ARM64: LeaveFrame
# ARM64-NOT: Frame
# ARM64-LABEL: end of function
